    "content" : "LEFT: Sea Cadets undergoing survival at sea training while on an annual year end camp at the SA Navy’s Seamanship School at SAS SIMONSBERG."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 408.898, 201.092, 541.446, 227.169 ],
    "font" : "Humanist521BT-Light",
    "font size" : 13.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0119935916736722, 0.3049973249435425, 0.6350042223930359]",
    "content" : "Where and when does the training take place?"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 51.02, 53.643, 209.94, 181.64 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 9.2,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "The Sea Cadet in South Africa movement traces its origins back to the first South African Training Ship (TS), located on Woodstock beach Cape Town, TS Woltemade was opened on 8 June 1905. The movement spread throughout South Africa and currently there are 15 training ships, nine are active and developing those values and skills required to ensure that the maritime industry is provided with recruits who have a passion for the sea."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 232.441, 168.648, 357.163, 184.13 ],
    "font" : "Humanist521BT-Light",
    "font size" : 13.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0119935916736722, 0.3049973249435425, 0.6350042223930359]",
    "content" : "Who are the Sea Cadets?"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 232.441, 52.451, 356.098, 159.252 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 9.2,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Sea Cadets are school going boys and girls from Grade 6 to Grade 12 who enjoy having “serious fun” while learning leadership, self-discipline and maritime orientated skills as a voluntary extra mural activity. Any youngster irrespective of race, gender or religion is welcome."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 408.898, 180.276, 529.933, 191.69 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 9.2,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "The land based training ships"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 391.178, 52.654, 528.911, 180.651 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 9.2,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "located around the country provide a safe space with competent instructors at which training can take place. Training takes place on Fridays or Saturdays or Sundays depending on the training ship involved, with leadership camps scheduled during the school holidays. The highlight of the year is the annual camp hosted by the SA Navy in Simon’s Town."
